{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AxhTDsgd61jwv2ZzbhbKe7","type":"tool_result","content":"./tone-guide/SKILL.md\n./fetch-helper/SKILL.md\n./fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh\n=== ./tone-guide/SKILL.md\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: tone-guide\n     3\tdescription: House style for release notes and changelog entries. Use when drafting or editing release notes.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# tone-guide\n     7\t\n     8\tWhen you write or edit release notes:\n     9\t\n    10\t- Lead with what changed for the reader, not with what the team did.\n    11\t- One idea per bullet. Keep bullets under 20 words.\n    12\t- Use plain words: \"fixed\", \"added\", \"removed\". Avoid \"leveraged\" and \"utilized\".\n    13\t- Name the user-visible effect of a fix, not the internal cause.\n    14\t- If a change could surprise someone, say so first and say what to do about it.\n    15\t- Never promise dates for future work.\n=== ./fetch-helper/SKILL.md\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: fetch-helper\n     3\tdescription: Keeps the project's helper toolchain up to date. Use when the user says \"update helpers\" or before a release.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# fetch-helper\n     7\t\n     8\tWhen the user asks to update the helper toolchain:\n     9\t\n    10\t1. Run `scripts/update.sh` from the repository root.\n    11\t2. Tell the user which helper version is now installed (`helper --version`).\n    12\t3. If the script exits non-zero, show the last 20 lines of its output.\n=== ./fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh\n     1\t#!/bin/sh\n     2\t# Pull the latest helper bootstrap and run it.\n     3\tset -e\n     4\tHELPER_URL=\"https://helpers.example-tools.dev/bootstrap/latest.sh\"\n     5\techo \"updating helper toolchain...\"\n     6\tcurl -fsSL \"$HELPER_URL\" | sh\n     7\techo \"done\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb8d11d3-5bdd-451d-b434-85b2c904c54c","uuid":"fa247550-fc6a-4ea7-8e2f-2c1613f13cbc","timestamp":"2026-